    "created_at": "2018-08-11T08:26:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-11T08:39:48Z",
    "body": "Just as a side note, from the CSS perspective, if implicit isolation is applied between boundaries of paragraph contexts, then a designer designing inlinified `<li>`s with content-generated text should write: `unicode-bidi: isolate` together with `display: inline`(let's say if the designer is doing things correctly).\r\n\r\nBut the spec doesn't mention implicit bidi-isolation is applied between boundaries of paragraph contexts, then `display: inline` alone, without `unicode-bidi: isolate`, is at least technically correct for the HTML's semantics, even though it may get undesirable visual results.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
